{
 "$schema": "com.minomobi.cad.assembly#v1",
 "name": "gripper-stroke",
 "_": "Parallel-jaw robot gripper, v7, links through the wall: ISO 9409-1-50-4-M6 flange → NEMA 17 pancake stepper with an integrated Tr8×2 screw → flange nut in a carriage on the floor → two 22 mm pivot arms keyed into it → four 40 mm links on bronze bushings that pass through the front wall’s two slots, over and under the MGN9 rail on its OUTER face, and pin onto the outside of each block → a 44 × 22 × 10 jaw carrier plate per side, four M4 and two Ø6 dowels for the customer’s finger. The stroke closes until the two jaw plates meet on the centre line. 88 × 44 × 70 mm case, the mechanism outside it 34 mm tall and reaching y = 90; mount centres 32 → 62 mm apart. The physical stroke: the screw is driven at 5 rpm, a screw mate moves the carriage 2 mm per turn (y = 44.35 open → 53.93 closed in 4.793 turns, 57.5 s), fixed mates carry the nut and the arms, and the links draw the jaws in by 15 mm each. Sweep with period 57.5 s; beyond it the nut runs on, as it would.",
 "params": {
